## When to split

- Over a limit in [02-size-and-structure.md]({{ref_02}}), **or**
- The code does more than one job, even below the limit. Signs:
  - its honest name needs "and" (`validateAndSaveOrder`),
  - mixed levels of abstraction (SQL next to business rules next to formatting),
  - several reasons to change it,
  - long parameter lists or nesting deeper than {{max_nesting}}.

## Find the pieces

1. Read the code and give each block a one-line label ("validate input", "compute price", "call payment API", "render table").
2. Each label is a candidate piece. Merge labels that always change together; keep apart labels that change for different reasons.
3. Name each piece per [01-naming.md]({{ref_01}}) — the label usually becomes the name.

## Where the pieces go

{{placement_rule}}
<!-- GEN: With clean-architecture: "Placement is decided by <link to clean-architecture 04>; follow its decision tree and smell table." Without it: the fallback — same module/feature, sibling files, no new top-level folders, ask before moving to shared. -->

## Move safely

- Update every caller and test; delete the old code; no re-export kept "so imports do not break".
- Behavior unchanged: refactor first, change logic in a separate step.
- Run the self-check ([05-self-check.md]({{ref_05}})) and the affected tests.

## Do not split

- One responsibility that reads linearly (mapping table, config, migration, generated code, prompt text).
- A piece under ~10 lines used once — keep it as a private function.
- A legacy file the phase does not touch.
- Never `part1`/`part2`/`helpers2`, never into shared just to shorten a file.

